;;; An int and a string with the same text are two activators — M1e2
;;; **W16**, register row `W16/int-and-string` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; fixed by S1e2.2.16 (2026-11-04). Promoted from
;;; `corpus/fuzz_findings/activator-text-key.ein` by the fix.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The stage file's program: one rule with two parameters, the relation
;;; `?R` to walk and the value `?f` to note, and two activators that differ
;;; only in their second argument, the int `1` and the string `"1"`. The
;;; loader holds those as two values, an int and a symbol whose text is
;;; `1`, so the KB has two `holds` facts. `activator-text-string-then-int.ein`
;;; is this file with the two activator lines swapped;
;;; `activator-text-int-only.ein` and `activator-text-string-only.ein` keep
;;; one activator each.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Each activator alone derives its own two `noted` facts: the int's
;;; `(noted 1 1)` and `(noted 2 1)`, the string's `(noted 1 "1")` and
;;; `(noted 2 "1")`. A rule set with one more activator cannot conclude
;;; less, so this file derives all four, in either order. H is empty, so R
;;; is `{∅}`: root, with the four.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered, and why it does not any more ─────────────
;;;
;;; Until S1e2.2.16 the compile key rendered a non-symbol argument as text
;;; and interned the text, so both activators keyed one plan, the first
;;; one's, and the string activator compiled nothing: root held the int's
;;; two `noted` facts and not the string's (`ein solve` and `ein saturate`
;;; at `6a775f3d`: `noted 2`, one plan), and a debug build aborted in
;;; `Engine::compile_all`'s check that its shortcut skipped no activator.
;;; The key is the activator's values since, so the two are two plans, and
;;; both orders derive the four in either build.
;;;
;;; ── What the claim can see ─────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A claim compares facts as printed, and the fact printer drops a
;;; string's quotes (P1e2.3's N5), so `(noted 1 1)` and `(noted 1 "1")` are
;;; one line to it: the claim below held before the fix too. What held the
;;; four is a count (`ein saturate`'s table, `noted 4`, the summary's
;;; `root.facts_by_relation`) and `rule_semantics.rs`'
;;; `an_int_and_a_string_with_one_text_are_two_activators`, which compares
;;; by value in both builds.

(relation edge  Node Node)
(relation holds Node)
(relation noted Node Node)

(rule note (?R ?f)
  :match  (and (?R ?a ?b) (holds ?f))
  :assert (noted ?a ?f))

(edge 1 2) (edge 2 3)
(holds 1)  (holds "1")

(note edge 1)
(note edge "1")

(solve
  ;; `holds` and `noted` are named, so both are closed: each state lists
  ;; their complete extent, root's facts included.
  :expect (region
            ;; state 1 of 1 — ∅, root itself · minimal · maximal
            (model (holds 1) (holds "1")
                   (noted 1 1) (noted 1 "1") (noted 2 1) (noted 2 "1"))))
